<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom">
<!-- Every RSS has a single channel. Here's ours: -->
<channel>
  <!-- Every channel is required to have a title, -->
  <!-- a link, and a description. -->
  <title>Site Status</title>
  <link>https://status.rapidcow.org</link>
  <description>Feed for status of www.rapidcow.org and
      other sites.</description>
  <!-- Link to documentation for RSS.                  -->
  <!-- To quote from the following linked site itself, -->
  <!-- "It's for people who might stumble across an    -->
  <!-- "RSS file on a Web server 25 years from now and -->
  <!-- wonder what it is."  Basically, it is a manual  -->
  <!-- for you: felow human.  Go read it! :)           -->
  <docs>https://www.rssboard.org/rss-specification</docs>
  <!-- lastBuildDate is not only relevant in the context of  -->
  <!-- generated RSS; it appears to be the last changed date -->
  <!-- simply, regardless of who it is changing it.          -->
  <!-- NOTE: with GNU date command, run !date ~~rfc~email    -->
  <lastBuildDate>Sun, 10 Nov 2024 03:33:03 -0600</lastBuildDate>
  <language>en-US</language>
  <!-- These are the email (name)s of people writing  -->
  <!-- content and managing the channel. I am both :) -->
  <managingEditor>webmaster@rapidcow.org</managingEditor>
  <webMaster>webmaster@rapidcow.org</webMaster>
  <!-- Lastly, we need to link to ourselves? -->
  <!-- This is a weird recommendation by W3: -->
  <!-- https://validator.w3.org/feed/docs/   -->
  <!--      warning/MissingAtomSelfLink.html -->
  <!-- It should be noted that atom:link is  -->
  <!-- in the atom namespace, declared above -->
  <!-- as http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom.       -->
  <atom:link rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"
      href="https://status.rapidcow.org/feed.xml" />
  <!-- Now the rest are just feed items! -->

  <item>
    <title>Plans for the end of 2024</title>
    <author>webmaster@rapidcow.org</author>
    <link>https://status.rapidcow.org/feed.html#1733566500</link>
    <guid>https://status.rapidcow.org/feed.html#1733566500</guid>
    <pubDate>Sun, 07 Dec 2024 04:15:00 -0600</pubDate>
    <description><![CDATA[
    <p>I got some more motivation to return to this and escape
    social media hellhole!  Thank you to my anonymous friend
    for being my FIRST subscriber outside of social media :)
    </p>
    <p>The plans are simple: www.rapidcow.org will get a landing
    page and a home page and www.endfind.me will get just a
    landing page that double as the home page.  (Don't visit
    either yet though, and if you do, don't be like <a href="https://twitter.com/AzzyThatMofo/status/1824128431245889679">Twitter</a>.)
    </p>
    <p>The exact date I'm unsure, but it should happen sometime
    between next week and the week after.  I'll let you know
    that when that happens.  Before that though I need to
    deal with them finals next week (ugh school... DX)
    </p>
    <p>Thanks.  I hope I can keep feeling this motivated.</p>
    ]]></description>
  </item>

